# Timeseries charts (`@infoplaza/platform/timeseries-charts`)

## Goal

Ship a **portable point-forecast chart** that other platforms can import without the map stack, ImWeather fetch layer, or app chrome. Charts are Recharts composed graphs. The models **catalog** is the timeseries catalog (`GET /api/platform/timeseries-models`, or `marine-timeseries-models` when `domain` is `marine`). Series load from `GET /api/platform/timeseries-point-forecast` (or `marine-timeseries-point-forecast`) unless the host passes `charts` / `getCharts`.

It is a **sibling product** to the timeseries table (`src/components/timeseries`) and ensemble. Own folder, own package export, own demo route (`/demo/timeseries-charts`). Do not nest it under the table folder or map, and do not re-export it from `src/components/index.ts`. Do not add `LINE` to `TimeseriesCellView`.

## What

A compound API. The models list is not host-supplied.

| Piece | Role |
|---|---|
| `TimeseriesModelsProvider` | Reused from timeseries. Required `lat`/`lon`. Optional `domain` (`land` default, or `marine`). Fetches `GET /api/platform/timeseries-models` or `marine-timeseries-models`. |
| `TimeseriesChartsForecast` | Packaged: ModelsProvider + Provider + optional Toolbar + Builder/Chart. Requires `lat`/`lon`. Footer is off (`showFooter` defaults to false). |
| `TimeseriesChartsProvider` | Holds selection (`model`, `run`, `visibleGroups`), charts. Reads the catalog from `TimeseriesModelsProvider`. Fetches point forecast when `charts` / `getCharts` are omitted. No `models` prop. |
| `TimeseriesChartsToolbar` | Model + run pills (catalog only) |
| `TimeseriesChartsBuilder` | Presentational: loading skeleton, one chart-block context per `TimeseriesChartBlock` |
| `TimeseriesChartsChart` | Reads the current block (or explicit graph props) and renders `TimeseriesGraph` |
| `TimeseriesChartsFooter` | Group-visibility pills. Disabled for now — do not mount in packaged or composed usage. |
| `TimeseriesGraph` | Low-level Recharts `ComposedChart` (LINE series; DIRECTION / VALUE / PRECIPITATION_TYPE in a strip band under the plot). PRECIPITATION_TYPE icons use the point-forecast palette colors (same visualization as the map legend). Hover values float in the title row and list every group item at the hovered hour. On a narrow plot (under 80px per forecast day) it shows one day at a time with a day pager; swipe the plot or tap a day chip. |

Config item views: `LINE`, `DIRECTION`, `VALUE`, `PRECIPITATION_TYPE`. One **group** = one composed chart. Builder stacks every group. Optional `thresholds` draws per-chart Y-lines and a status strip from `conditions` + `ignored_hours`. Optional `line` on a LINE item sets color, strokeWidth, strokeDasharray, opacity, and curve (`linear` | `monotone` | `step` | `stepAfter` | `stepBefore`). Optional `yAxis.domain` on a group sets the shared Y scale (`number` | `auto` | `dataMin` | `dataMax`); omit to keep `[0, auto]`. `TimeseriesChartGraphConfig.domain` is the **X-axis time range**, not Y.

## How

Import only from `@infoplaza/platform/timeseries-charts`. Wrap host UI in `.ip-platform` and use `ip:` utilities.

**Packaged** — default chrome on; hide with flags. `lat` and `lon` are required. Charts load from the point-forecast endpoint unless `charts` / `getCharts` is passed. `domain` defaults to `land`:

```tsx
<TimeseriesChartsForecast
  lat={52.3676}
  lon={4.9041}
  model="gfs"
  showToolbar={false}
/>
```

Marine:

```tsx
<TimeseriesChartsForecast
  lat={55.551448725742}
  lon={4.0444930642829116}
  domain="marine"
/>
```

**Composed** — host wraps `TimeseriesModelsProvider`; `TimeseriesChartsProvider` has no `models` prop:

```tsx
<TimeseriesModelsProvider lat={52.3676} lon={4.9041}>
  <TimeseriesChartsProvider>
    <TimeseriesChartsToolbar />
    <TimeseriesChartsBuilder>
      <TimeseriesChartsChart />
    </TimeseriesChartsBuilder>
  </TimeseriesChartsProvider>
</TimeseriesModelsProvider>
```

Selection is hybrid: `model` + `onModelChange` (controlled) or `model` without `onModelChange` / `defaultModel` / omit (provider-owned preferred slug). Same for `run` and `visibleGroups`. Unknown slugs fall back to the first catalog model; unknown runtimes are clamped to the catalog. If `charts` is passed it wins; otherwise `getCharts({ model, run, models, elementGroups, visibleGroups, locale, timezone })` is used when provided; otherwise the Provider fetches point-forecast charts. `elementGroups` defaults from `domain`: `DEFAULT_LAND_TIMESERIES_CHART_GROUPS` or `DEFAULT_MARINE_TIMESERIES_CHART_GROUPS`. Fetch once per runtime for all groups; do not N+1 by group. `plotHeight` defaults to 320 (`DEFAULT_TIMESERIES_CHART_PLOT_HEIGHT`); set it on Forecast or Provider so Chart/Graph and the Builder loading skeleton share it. Chart/Graph can override. `fixedHeight` still overrides the total Recharts container. `hourInterval` defaults to 6 (`DEFAULT_TIMESERIES_CHART_HOUR_INTERVAL`); allowed values are `1`, `3`, or `6`. It draws unlabeled vertical hour lines (day ticks stay on the X axis). For `3` and `6`, DIRECTION / VALUE / PRECIPITATION_TYPE strip overlays show the latest point in each bucket, centered in the cell; `1` keeps every overlay timestamp. LINE series stay hourly. Set it on Forecast or Provider so Chart/Graph share it. Chart/Graph can override. The hover header lists LINE values, DIRECTION (arrow + degrees + compass), VALUE, and PRECIPITATION_TYPE at the hovered hour (exact timestamp; not the 3h/6h strip summary). `thresholds` is optional (`conditions` + `ignored_hours`). Each chart keeps AND-groups whose `elementId`s are all LINE series on that chart; it draws dashed Y-lines and a status strip above the date labels. Chart/Graph can override. Optional `line` on LINE items and `yAxis` on groups copy onto the graph config. Graph `domain` remains the X-axis time range; Y-axis domain is `yAxis.domain` or `[0, auto]`. When the plot is narrower than about 80px per forecast day, Chart/Graph window the X domain to one calendar day (default today). Builder shows one sticky day pager for the stack so every chart stays on the same day; standalone Graph shows its own pager. Compact hover values wrap under the title; the X axis labels hours (`HH:mm`). Wide plots keep the full domain.

Demo patterns live in `demo-next/components/timeseries-charts/` (packaged, hour-interval, thresholds, marine, chart-only, composed, custom-elements, custom-styling). Prefer updating those examples over inventing a fourth usage mode. `elementGroups` replaces domain defaults when defined; it does not merge.

## Rules

- **Catalog is API-only.** Do not pass a `models` array into Provider or Forecast. `TimeseriesModelsProvider` is the only writer. `domain` (`land` | `marine`) lives on ModelsProvider / packaged Forecast, not on TimeseriesChartsProvider.
- **Provider loads charts by default.** Shape `TimeseriesChartBlock[]` (title + graph config). `charts` / `getCharts` remain a host override. Do not import ImWeather BFF routes.
- **Reuse table fetch, not table rows.** Use `fetchTimeseriesPointForecast` / `findTimeseriesSeries` / `partitionTimeseriesGroupItems`. Do not reuse `assembleBlock`, `TimeseriesTable`, or `EnsembleGraph`.
- **`run === 'all'`:** the Provider fetches one point-forecast request per catalog runtime and stacks all group charts for each runtime, with `subtitle` set to the formatted runtime.
- **Builder does not fetch.** It maps context `charts` onto Chart. The Provider fetches point forecast.
- **Toolbar** resolves `props ?? context` and returns `null` if neither exists — do not throw. Footer group pills exist but are off for now (`showFooter` defaults to false; do not mount `TimeseriesChartsFooter` in demos). `useTimeseriesCharts()` throws outside the provider; `useTimeseriesChartsContext()` is nullable for standalone pieces.
- **Keep map, timeseries table, and charts separate.** No charts in the timeseries or map barrels. Toolbar/footer reuse timeseries pills internally, not map controls. Coordinates live on `TimeseriesModelsProvider` (and packaged Forecast), not as props on `TimeseriesChartsProvider`.
- **Stay presentational.** No next-intl, next-auth, `#main-header` sticky offsets, or paywall chrome. Titles and group labels are already-resolved strings. Locale is for date axis labels (`en`/`nl`/`de`/`it`/`es`/`fr`).
- **Out of scope:** ICON on charts, dual Y-axis, renaming `TimeseriesChart`, nesting under the table package.
